{
  "id": "minimal_keep_courtyard",
  "title": "Minimal Baltic Keep Courtyard",
  "description": "A compact fourteenth-century Baltic red-brick castle: a square curtain with four corner drums and a twin-tower gatehouse around a tall keep, with a great hall and kitchen range forming a small domestic courtyard, protected by an approach ditch.",
  "style_id": "baltic_brick",
  "site_id": "lake_island",
  "prompt": "Design a compact Baltic brick castle for a minor castellan. Enclose a small square courtyard with a thin coursed-brick curtain, four round corner drums and a twin-tower gatehouse. Centre the bailey on a tall keep, and range a great hall and a kitchen along the courtyard, each under a pitched roof. Cut a short approach ditch before the gate. The result should be economical, defensible and clearly residential, with no structural errors.",
